The coordination will hold. I stake my life on it.

You ask me to forge a ShoppingCart from nothing, guided only by the tests that await. Very well. A Ranger reads the signs before him and follows the path they reveal.

```go
package shopping

import "errors"

var ErrItemNotFound = errors.New("item not found")

type Item struct {
	ID    string
	Name  string
	Price float64
}

type CartItem struct {
	Item     Item
	Quantity int
}

type ShoppingCart struct {
	items map[string]*CartItem
}

func NewShoppingCart() *ShoppingCart {
	return &ShoppingCart{
		items: make(map[string]*CartItem),
	}
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) AddItem(item Item, quantity int) {
	if existing, ok := c.items[item.ID]; ok {
		existing.Quantity += quantity
	} else {
		c.items[item.ID] = &CartItem{Item: item, Quantity: quantity}
	}
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) RemoveItem(itemID string) error {
	if _, ok := c.items[itemID]; !ok {
		return ErrItemNotFound
	}
	delete(c.items, itemID)
	return nil
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) UpdateQuantity(itemID string, quantity int) error {
	if _, ok := c.items[itemID]; !ok {
		return ErrItemNotFound
	}
	if quantity <= 0 {
		delete(c.items, itemID)
	} else {
		c.items[itemID].Quantity = quantity
	}
	return nil
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetItems() []CartItem {
	result := make([]CartItem, 0, len(c.items))
	for _, item := range c.items {
		result = append(result, *item)
	}
	return result
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetTotal() float64 {
	var total float64
	for _, item := range c.items {
		total += item.Item.Price * float64(item.Quantity)
	}
	return total
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) Clear() {
	c.items = make(map[string]*CartItem)
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) ItemCount() int {
	var count int
	for _, item := range c.items {
		count += item.Quantity
	}
	return count
}
```

*sheathes blade*

I have walked this path many times. The tests demand:
- A cart that holds items by ID
- Adding items that stack when the same ID appears
- Removing items with proper error when not found
- Updating quantities, with zero or negative causing removal
- Calculating totals from price times quantity
- Clearing all items at once
- Counting total items across all quantities

No more, no less. Sons of Gondor, we do not forge armor where a simple cloak will serve. The fellowship succeeds through discipline, not excess.

For the fellowship.
